% M8-bits-encoding-T3 continuation (D-0134 section 8): int_eq_reif / int_ne_reif over bits.
% At `--bits-above 0` x, y, z are on bits and the two [Clause] pieces of the reified
% equality are DERIVED: rows A and B of its guarded `_neN` pair, each with the bridges of
% the fixed terms and the reifier as one more term, saturated and summed so the selector
% resolves away. Deciding b = 0 and then y = 2 makes x <> 2 through b <-> (x = y): an
% interior hole in a bits domain (x is in 0..4 by x <= y + 2), the reifier's literal in its
% clause. x is then decided at its top, 4, and d <-> (x <> 4) has its condition ENTAILED
% with d open: the entailment piece pushes d to 0, a derived line whose reifier term
% carries the negation of the claim. The rows faces (LE/GE, [Linear]) push e to 0. The
% search lands on b = 0, y = 2, x = 4, z = 1, e = 0, d = 0.
var 0..9: x :: output_var;
var 0..9: y :: output_var;
var 0..9: z :: output_var;
var bool: b :: output_var;
var bool: e :: output_var;
var bool: d :: output_var;
constraint int_eq_reif(x, y, b);
constraint int_lin_le([1, -1], [x, y], 2);
constraint int_lin_le([-1], [y], -2);
constraint int_eq_reif(x, z, e);
constraint int_lin_eq([1], [z], 1);
constraint int_ne_reif(x, 4, d);
solve :: seq_search([int_search([b, y], input_order, indomain_min, complete), int_search([x], input_order, indomain_max, complete)]) satisfy;
